{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>Today.</b> He mentioned at the outset: no leavened bread shall be eaten, and so you shall do for all generations, just as you did on the day you went out, and just as this occurred at the time when the aviv is present, so shall you do every year when the aviv is present in the land of Israel. This is the aviv of barley, and the meaning of aviv is like בִכּור (firstfruit), for it derives from the root אב, which is like firstborn to one who has begotten, or a sage to a student he has taught. And it is written: for the barley is aviv (above 9:31), and the proof is that he said of the festival of Shavuot: firstfruits of the wheat harvest (below 34:22)."], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 13, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:34:04.359296389Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}